course: dictionary
lesson: 6789
title: Words from space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one subject, like science or maps. When you meet one, the words around it give you clues. «Thousands of old satellites and pieces of rocket orbit Earth as space junk.» Orbit suggests something going round Earth, so orbital must be about that kind of path.
explain: Orbital means to do with an orbit, the path something follows as it goes round a planet, star or moon. Ask yourself: what is going round what? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Even a paint fleck at orbital speed can damage a spacecraft.» Here orbital speed means the speed of something moving along its orbit. A tiny fleck of paint can do damage at that speed, which tells you it is very fast.
fact: Orbital means to do with an orbit, the path of something going round a planet, star or moon.
fact: «Orbit» is the key word inside «orbital», so look for it when you meet either word.
fact: An orbital road goes round a city, like London's M25.
fact: The orbital bone is the bony cup around the eye.
fact: In science, an orbital is a region in an atom where electrons are found. The same word can mean different things in different subjects, so check the subject around it.
exercise: «Thousands of old satellites and pieces of rocket orbit Earth as space junk.» What does orbit mean here? | *Travel round Earth along a path | Shine very brightly | Break into tiny pieces on the ground | Sink into the sea
exercise: An orbital road goes round a city, like London's M25. What is an orbital road? | A very narrow path up a hill | A road under the sea | A road made of gold | *A road that goes round a city
exercise: The orbital bone is the bony cup around the eye. Where is the orbital bone? | Along the spine | *Around the eye | In the foot | Inside the ear
test: «A paint fleck at orbital speed can damage a spacecraft.» What does orbital speed relate to? | Cooking food quickly | Swimming across a lake | The speed of a car in a city traffic jam | *The speed of something moving along its orbit
test: Maya says orbital only means a bone around the eye. What is the best answer? | No, orbital means very slow | Yes, orbital only ever means a bone | No, orbital means a kind of food | *Orbital has several meanings, so the subject around the word tells you which one
exam: Which subject would use the word orbital to mean the path of a satellite round Earth? | Art | Music | Cooking | *Science
